======================================================================
STORE-SPECIFIC DATA MODEL
======================================================================

The interactive parser should produce a standard internal purchase record.

Use this canonical structure:

{
    "six_digit_sku": "... or NA",
    "product": "... or NA",
    "tax_code": "... or NA",
    "price": "... or NA",
    "store_number": "...",
    "date": "MM/DD/YYYY"
}

All stores ultimately map into this same schema.

Never omit fields.

Use:

"NA"

when the information does not apply or cannot be determined.

----------------------------------------------------------------------
PUBLIX
----------------------------------------------------------------------

Publix purchase information consists of:

- Product
- Tax Code
- Price
- Store Number
- Date

Publix generally does NOT provide the six-digit Aldi-style SKU required by
our canonical schema.

Therefore:

six_digit_sku = "NA"

Publix tax codes currently supported:

F
    Food item.

    In most states where Publix operates, such as Florida, basic grocery
    items and raw foods are generally exempt from state sales tax.
    This code also commonly identifies food eligible for SNAP/EBT.

T
    Taxable item.

    Typically used for taxable non-food items, such as household products,
    or certain prepared foods.

TF
    Taxable Food.

LF
    Local Tax Food.

TLF
    Taxable / Local Tax Food.

Keep these descriptions available to the user during manual correction.

Do NOT attempt to infer tax law beyond these supplied codes.

If a Publix tax code cannot confidently be identified:

tax_code = "NA"

----------------------------------------------------------------------
TRADER JOE'S
----------------------------------------------------------------------

Trader Joe's purchase information currently consists of:

- Product
- Price
- Store Number
- Date

Therefore:

six_digit_sku = "NA"
tax_code = "NA"

----------------------------------------------------------------------
ALDI
----------------------------------------------------------------------

Aldi purchase information currently consists of:

- Six-Digit SKU
- Product
- Price
- Store Number
- Date

The SKU must be exactly six digits when present.

For the canonical schema:

tax_code may be populated if it is clearly available in the OCR input;
otherwise use "NA".

Do not invent or repair an uncertain SKU during this stage.

