======================================================================
HOW PURCHASE HISTORY SHOULD GROW
======================================================================

When a new accepted purchase is committed:

Try to locate an existing product-history row.

Use conservative matching.

Preferred identity rules:

ALDI:
    Primary identity:
        Six-Digit SKU + Store Number

    If SKU == "NA":
        Product + Store Number

PUBLIX:
    Product + Store Number

TRADER JOE'S:
    Product + Store Number

OTHER:
    Six-Digit SKU + Product + Store Number where available.

Do not fuzzy-match product names in this first implementation.

Exact normalized matching is safer.

Normalization may include:

- trimming surrounding whitespace
- case-insensitive comparison

Do not spell-correct product names.

If an existing row is found:

Find the next unused Date N / Price N pair and append the new purchase.

Example existing row:

Six-Digit SKU | Product | Tax Code | Store Number | Date 1     | Price 1
NA            | Milk    | F        | 1058         | 08/25/2026 | 4.99

Next purchase becomes:

Six-Digit SKU | Product | Tax Code | Store Number | Date 1     | Price 1 | Date 2     | Price 2
NA            | Milk    | F        | 1058         | 08/25/2026 | 4.99    | 09/02/2026 | 5.19

If no matching history row exists:

Create a new row.

